"type":"text","text":"order (by vertex index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering"},{"type":"text","text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"degeneracy d."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques":{"title":"Cliques","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","type":"topic","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/cliques","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques/Element":{"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/element","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Element"}],"type":"topic","title":"MaximalCliques.Element","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Element"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/Element","role":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph/Vertex":{"abstract":[],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph\/vertex","title":"Vertex","fragments":[{"